an ownership CODE in place of an exact percentage.~  OWNERSHIP CODE TABLE - the code, the disclosure RANGE it stands for, and the PERCENTAGE to emit*~  - NA  Less Than 5%            -^gt! 4.99~  - A   5% But Less Than 10%    -^gt! 6.00~  - B   10% But Less Than 25%   -^gt! 11.00~  - C   25% But Less Than 50%   -^gt! 25.01~  - D   50% But Less Than 75%   -^gt! 50.01~  - E   75% or More             -^gt! 75.01~  THE RANGE SAYS WHAT THE CODE MEANS! THE PERCENTAGE IS WHAT YOU EMIT. The range tells you what the form disclosed - a "D" means a holding of at least 50% and under 75% - and the PERCENTAGE column is the deemed figure that goes into actualOwnershipPercentage. Never emit a range, a bound, or any figure of your own choosing from inside the range* the percentage column is the only value this clause produces.~  THIS TABLE IS THE WHOLE RULE. Every holder carrying a code takes its own row, INDEPENDENTLY of who else holds a code in the same target. There are no combination cases and nothing to look up b','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
