gure, never a presumed band.~  AN ADV OWNERSHIP CODE FEEDS THE VOTING FIELD THROUGH §9.2.2 V3. The code is an OWNERSHIP disclosure and states nothing about votes, so it never reaches actualVotingRightsPercentage as evidence - but §9.2.2''s ladder deems the voting figure from whatever supplied the ownership figure, and a resolved band is such a supply. Where no document states the voting position, actualVotingRightsPercentage = the band emitted for this link (a D holder takes 50.01 in both fields), VotingBasis=[V3 deemed from ownership], and no MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS is emitted. Where a document DOES state voting, or states this holding is non-voting, V1 or V2 governs and the band is irrelevant to the voting field.~  DO NOT LOG A GAP THAT DOES NOT EXIST. Where a code is RESOLVED and a band assigned, do NOT emit MISSING_PERCENTAGE, do NOT add a SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry, and do NOT raise a rule 15 advisory for the OWNERSHIP percentage, solely because the form printed a band rather than an exact figure. Th','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
