    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('because a percentage the extractor computed or re-rounded is indistinguishable, in the output, from one the document printed, and because a set of such figures no longer totals what the document totals.~  THREE PROVENANCES FOR AN OWNERSHIP FIGURE, AND THERE IS NO FOURTH. Every value emitted in actualOwnershipPercentage is one of*~  - P1 PRINTED - the figure printed for THIS owner-and-target pair, transcribed digit for digit!~  - P2 ASSIGNED BY A DEFINED CLAUSE - §9.2''s wholly-owned wordings and §9.2.1''s resolved "WO" code (each exactly 100), and §9.2.3''s resolved Form ADV code (its table row)!~  - P3 ABSENT - 0 with MISSING_PERCENTAGE in this record''s qaFlags and the SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry per OC.3.~  A VOTING FIGURE HAS A FOURTH PROVENANCE, AND EXACTLY ONE. actualVotingRightsPercentage takes P1 (a stated voting figure - §9.2.2 V1), P3 (nothing to deem from - §9.2.2 V4), an EVIDENCED ZERO (§9.2.2 V2), or*~  - P4 DEEMED - §9.2.2 V3 carries this record''s actualOwnershipPercentage into the voting field where no document states the voting position. P4 is available to the VOTING field alone and to no other* nothing is ever deemed into actualOwnershipPercentage, which keeps its three provenances and no more. A deemed figure is a copy, never a calculation - it is the ownership figure unchanged, so it inherits that figure''s precision and is not re-rounded.~  A figure reached any other way is a CALCULATED figure and KERNEL C bars it. Barred whatever the arithmetic looks like* a residual (100 minus the holders you already have), an apportionment of a block among the parties inside it (§9.0A), a rescaling of a set so that it reconciles to 100, a share count divided by a total, and a printed figure re-rounded to a tidier number. Calculation belongs to dilutionOwnershipPercentage and dilutionVotingRightsPercentage alone (§12.3 / §12.4) and appears nowhere else in a record.~  TRANSCRIBE EVERY DIGIT THE DOCUMENT PRINTS. 33.333 is emitted as 33.333, 8.9 as 8.9, 52.27 as 52.27. Do not round, truncate or pad a printed figure to two decimal places. §12.4''s "report rounded half-up to 2 decimal places" is scoped to the two dilution fields and to them alone* applied to a direct percentage it changes evidence by a hundredth on one record, and across a shareholder set it moves that target''s §9.3 total off the figure the document supports - which is how a correctly extracted structure comes to total 100.1% or 100.001%.~  A SHARE COUNT IS NOT A PERCENTAGE. Where a source states holdings as numbers of shares and prints no percentage for the pair, the percentage is P3* 0 with MISSING_PERCENTAGE, the SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry, and a rule 15 advisory requesting the percentages. Do not divide the holding by an issued-share figure, and above all do not divide it by the total of the holdings you happened to find - that forces the set to exactly 100 and manufactures a reconciliation out of nothing, concealing whatever is missing. Nor does §9.2.2 help h','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
