RCENTAGE_CONFLICT in the qaFlags of T''s records, record a data gap naming T and the computed excess, raise a rule 15 advisory, and state all three in governanceBasis part [6]. Do NOT wait for 105%* 95-105% is the band inside which the set is the right SIZE, never a licence to absorb an unexplained overshoot that happens to sit inside it.~  - A target whose shareholders carry unknown percentages (MISSING_PERCENTAGE, or an ORBIS "MO" designation per rule 6) is exempt from the sum check* record the exemption rather than compute a false sum.~  - The explicitly-partial-source exemption requires positive evidence, not silence* it applies only where the source itself states the list is partial, extracted, or illustrative! where the document is by its nature a single-holder instrument (a single share certificate, an excerpt naming one holder)! or where the source is a Form ADV ownership-code table (§9.2.3). A Form ADV Schedule A / Schedule B discloses holders down to a threshold band and not below it, so such a ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('table is BY ITS NATURE a partial list and satisfies this category BY RULE - no printed statement of partiality need be found, and a single E holder totalling 75.01 is NOT an incomplete shareholder set. Name it as explicitly-partial-source with the Form ADV basis stated. Record in governanceBasis WHICH exemption applied (unknown-percentage, or explicitly-partial-source) and why - an unexplained exemption is not permitted.~  - A TARGET WHOSE ENTIRE SHAREHOLDER SET IS ONE 100% HOLDER PASSES THIS CHECK BY CONSTRUCTION, so passing certifies nothing about it. A single 100% link sums to exactly 100 whether or not the link is real, which makes a wholly-owned edge the one link this gate cannot catch - and an invented intermediate layer is normally invented in exactly that shape. Where T has exactly one recorded holder and that holder is at 100%, do not treat the sum as corroboration. Require instead that the record''s evidenceSnippet state the 100% - or a §9.2 / §9.2.1 wholly-owned wording - for THAT owner-and-target PAIR specifically, quoted from the document, to the same standard §9.2.1 imposes on a "WO" code. A quote that names only one of the two parties, or that states the figure for a different pair, does not evidence this link* emit 0 with MISSING_PERCENTAGE and the SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE gap per OC.3, and do not record T''s set as complete.~  - TARGETSUM IS COMPUTED FROM THE RECORDS YOU ARE ABOUT TO EMIT, NEVER ASSERTED. Before writing rule 18''s TargetSum token for a record, add up the actualOwnershipPercentage of the records whose linkedName is that target - the same records, in the same output - and write THAT figure. Do not write the figure the source suggests the set ought to reach, do not write 100 because a complete set would total 100, and do not carry a sum forward from a previous run or a previous draft of this output. A TargetSum that disagrees with the emitted records is the most damaging token in the reasoning string* it reports