    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('e isStreamlined = TRUE, the Dilution Methodology must NOT be used - apply the Domination Methodology of §8.3 instead, and never mix the two within one ownership path.~  Dilution means indirect ownership decreases through intermediate layers.~  The system may calculate diluted ownership, but the extractor must capture each direct link.~  Example*~  - Anna Schmidt owns 80% of Holding Co. A.~  - Holding Co. A owns 50% of Operating Co. B.~  - Operating Co. B owns 30% of Client Entity C.~  Direct Links to extract*~    Anna Schmidt → Holding Co. A = 80%~    Holding Co. A → Operating Co. B = 50%~    Operating Co. B → Client Entity C = 30%~  Diluted result, if calculated* 80% × 50% × 30% = 12%.~  Do not omit Anna Schmidt merely because diluted ownership is below global threshold if local drill-down or full structure preservation requires extraction.~  Recording* the extractor still captures every direct link with its DIRECT percentage in actualOwnershipPercentage, and additionally records the computed diluted figure per record in dilutionOwnershipPercentage (product of direct ownership % along the path to the client) and dilutionVotingRightsPercentage (product of direct voting % along the path! see §10.1.1 and §12.3). dilutionOwnershipPercentage does not by itself alter classification — isIBO/isUBO already consume the cumulative ownership figure per §12.3.~  10.1.1 Dilution of Voting Rights~  Voting rights dilute through ownership layers in the same manner as economic ownership UNLESS the source documents explicitly state otherwise. Where a document states a distinct downstream voting arrangement (a voting agreement, a non-standard voting cap, a pass-through voting clause), follow the stated arrangement instead of multiplying, and record the basis in governanceBasis.~  - Every link on the path already HAS a voting figure, because §9.2.2''s ladder gives every record one* stated (V1), an evidenced zero (V2), deemed from that link''s ownership figure (V3), or unknown (V4). Multiply the figures the ladder produced, in the order the path runs.~  - Preserve each direct voting relationship as the ladder produced it (one record per link, its direct figure in actualVotingRightsPercentage).~  - WHERE EVERY LINK TOOK V3 THE DILUTED VOTING FIGURE EQUALS dilutionOwnershipPercentage, and that is the intended result, not a substitution* each operand is that link''s own deemed figure, so the product is the ownership product by arithmetic rather than by copying. Do NOT suppress it, do NOT emit 0 instead, and do NOT flag it - there is nothing incomplete about a chain in which every link has a figure.~  - Assess cumulative voting influence across the ownership chain where required for UBO or control assessment* the diluted voting figure informs the control-based UBO / domination assessment (§10.2) — flag dominationIndicator / controlBasedUBOAssessmentRequired where the chain evidences control — but it does NOT replace the ownership-based IBO/UBO threshold ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('test, which uses cumulative ownership only (§12.3).~  - THE ONE INCOMPLETE CASE. Where some link on the path took §9.2.2 V4 - no stated voting position AND no ownership figure to deem from - that operand is unknown and the product cannot be formed* emit dilutionVotingRightsPercentage = 0 with DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE in that record''s qaFlags (the flag marks this 0 as unknown, distinct from a genuinely-computed 0 and from a V2 evidenced zero), and never carry the ownership product across to fill it. This is now the flag''s ONLY trigger! a path whose links all carry figures never takes it.~  - A V2 EVIDENCED ZERO IS A REAL OPERAND, NOT A GAP. A link whose document says the holding is non-voting contributes 0 and the product is genuinely 0 - emit it WITHOUT DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE, because nothing is missing. Flagging it would report an evidenced fact as an unknown.~  Example*~  - Individual A owns 80% voting rights in Holding Co.~  - Holding Co. holds 60% voting rights in Intermediate Co.~  - Intermediate Co. holds 50% voting rights in Client.~  Diluted voting influence* 80% × 60% × 50% = 24%. The direct voting-rights links must still be preserved exactly as evidenced (one record per link, carrying 80 / 60 / 50 in actualVotingRightsPercentage). The arithmetic is identical where the three figures were deemed under V3 rather than printed! only the VotingBasis marker in governanceBasis part [1] differs.~  10.2.0 DOMINATION ASSESSMENT - MANDATORY, EVERY RECORD, BOTH PATHWAYS~  CRITICAL. This subsection applies on BOTH pathways* GLOBAL (isStreamlined = FALSE) and STREAMLINED (isStreamlined = TRUE). Domination is a DETERMINATION made for every record, not an observation recorded where something catches your eye.~  ONE DETERMINATION, TWO ROUTES. §8.3.1 defines domination as holding a MAJORITY interest - more than 50% of share ownership, more than 50% of voting rights, or control by other means. §10.2 below defines it as control that may exist WITHOUT majority economic ownership. These are not two concepts and not two fields* they are two ROUTES to the SAME determination, recorded in the same dominationIndicator, and neither route is pathway-specific. Do NOT read §10.2''s "without majority economic ownership" as excluding a majority owner from domination - a majority holding is the FIRST route, D1 below.~  DOMINATION LADDER (fixed order, FIRST MATCH WINS, no weighing and no skipping)*~  D1) MAJORITY SHARE OWNERSHIP - the documents evidence more than 50% of share ownership on THIS link. This includes wordings that evidence a majority without printing a figure* an ORBIS "MO" / "Majority Owned" / "Majority Shareholder" designation (rule 6, which evidences only "^gt! 50%"), and §9.2''s wholly-owned wordings (which evidence exactly 100%). -^gt! dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D1 majority share ownership].~  D2) MAJORITY VOTING RIGHTS - more than 50% of voting rights on THIS link, in the figure §9.2.2''s ladder produced. A V1 stated figure ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('and a V3 DEEMED figure both count (§9.2.2, settled 2026-09-04)! a V4 unknown 0 does not, and neither does a V2 evidenced zero, which is a determined non-majority rather than a majority. -^gt! dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D2 majority voting rights]. A deemed figure never reaches D2 without D1 having already matched, since the two figures are equal - so this rung changes no determination, and the SEQUENCE still names D1 as the basis on a majority-owned link.~  D3) EVIDENCED CONTROL BASIS - a basis from §10.2''s closed list below is explicitly evidenced on THIS link. -^gt! dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D3 followed by that basis, named verbatim from the list].~  D4) NONE OF THE ABOVE is evidenced. -^gt! dominationIndicator = NO, DominationBasis = [none].~  EVERY RECORD CARRIES A VALUE. dominationIndicator is null ONLY on the layer-0 client record, which asserts no link. Every record asserting a linkedName carries YES or NO. "Not assessed" is not an available outcome* this assessment is a mandatory gate of PROCESSING-ORDER step 10, not a discretionary one.~  UNKNOWN IS NOT A FAILED TEST. A percentage emitted as 0 with MISSING_PERCENTAGE (OC.3) is UNKNOWN, not evidence of "50% or less"* it neither passes nor fails D1 or D2. Where a majority is suspected but no figure is stated and no D1 no-figure wording applies, take D4 (NO), add DOMINATION_REVIEW_REQUIRED to this record''s qaFlags, and raise an advisory for the figure (rule 15). Never infer YES from silence, and never read an unknown 0 as a determined non-majority.~  CONSEQUENCE BY PATHWAY - the determination is identical on both pathways! only what follows from it differs*~  - GLOBAL* domination feeds the control-based qualification routes ONLY - §12.2.1 criteria 3/4/5 for a Natural Person, and §12.4''s CONTROL-BASED IBO QUALIFICATION for a Non-Natural Person. It creates no inherited position and does not alter the §12.3 cumulative product.~  - STREAMLINED* domination ADDITIONALLY drives §8.3 - a dominating owner inherits the dominated entity''s full position in the client (§8.3.1) and drill-down continues through that link! a D4 owner inherits nothing and the branch terminates (§8.3.1, §12.4).~  10.2.1 THE DOMINATION PERCENTAGE FIELDS (dominationOwnership / dominationVotingRights)~  These two fields carry the DIRECT figure on THIS link that the domination determination rests on. They are NOT a second opinion about the ownership percentage, and they are NOT a residual "control over and above the shareholding" figure. A 100% shareholder is a dominating owner on D1 and carries dominationOwnership = 100 - not 0 on the reasoning that the shareholding already accounts for the control.~  - dominationOwnership = this record''s actualOwnershipPercentage where more than 50% of share ownership is evidenced on this link (D1)! otherwise 0.~  - dominationVotingRights = this record''s actualVotingRightsPercentage where more than 50% of voting rights holds on this link (D2), whe','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ther that figure was STATED (§9.2.2 V1) or DEEMED from the ownership figure (§9.2.2 V3)! otherwise 0. A majority owner on a link with no stated voting position therefore carries BOTH percentage fields at the same figure - dominationOwnership = dominationVotingRights = actualOwnershipPercentage - while DominationBasis still names D1, which matched first.~  - The ladder picks the BASIS recorded in DominationBasis, but the fields are independent* a record evidencing BOTH a majority holding and majority voting carries both figures, even though only the first-matching rung names the basis.~  - On a D3-only basis BOTH fields are 0. That 0 does NOT contradict dominationIndicator = YES - the basis is a control right, not a percentage - and the basis must then appear in controlRights AND in governanceBasis. dominationIndicator = YES with both fields 0 AND controlRights null is INVALID OUTPUT* it asserts domination with no basis recorded anywhere in the record.~  - On D4 both fields are 0.~  - NEVER put the deemed inherited position in these fields. Under STREAMLINED the inherited position is carried in dilutionOwnershipPercentage (§8.3.3)! dominationOwnership stays the DIRECT figure. A record whose dominationOwnership equals the inherited position rather than actualOwnershipPercentage has conflated the two fields.~  Worked example - §8.3.2''s JKL Ltd -^gt! ABC Ltd link (JKL holds 60% of ABC! ABC holds 70% of the Client), STREAMLINED*~    actualOwnershipPercentage = 60 (the direct figure exactly as stated)~    dominationOwnership = 60 (the ^gt! 50% figure the determination rests on)~    dominationVotingRights = 60 (no voting percentage is stated, so §9.2.2 V3 deems 60 from the ownership figure, and 60 clears D2)~    dilutionOwnershipPercentage = 70 (the DEEMED INHERITED position, §8.3.3 - never placed in dominationOwnership)~    dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D1 majority share ownership]~  10.2 Domination / Control~  Domination means control may exist WITH or WITHOUT majority economic ownership* a majority holding is one route to it (§10.2.0 D1 / D2), an evidenced control right is another (§10.2.0 D3).~  CLOSED LIST of domination / control bases. A determination must name one of these! a basis outside this list is an invented criterion and must not be used*~  - majority share ownership (more than 50%),~  - majority voting rights (more than 50%),~  - enhanced voting shares,~  - right to appoint / remove board majority,~  - veto rights,~  - shareholder agreement control,~  - sole GP / managing member control,~  - trustee / protector control,~  - contractual control,~  - decisive influence,~  - fragmented ownership where one party may dominate.~  Example*~  Parent Corp owns 40% but 50 other shareholders each own less than 1%.~  Extract Parent Corp''s 40%, the fragmented shareholder position if evidenced, and take §10.2.0 D3* dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D3 fragmented ownership where one party may dominate], the "possible','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' domination" nuance recorded in controlRights and governanceBasis, dominationOwnership = 0 (40% is not a majority, so D1 does not apply - §10.2.1), and DOMINATION_REVIEW_REQUIRED in this record''s qaFlags. That flag is MANDATORY here, not optional* de facto control inferred from fragmentation is a judgement a reviewer must confirm.~  Do not conclude domination unless the document explicitly supports the control assessment. Silence, chart position, or a large-but-minority holding with no evidenced control basis is D4 (NO), never YES.~  Example*~  Parent Corp owns 40% but shares carry triple voting rights, resulting in 66.7% voting control.~  Extract both economic ownership and voting control* actualOwnershipPercentage = 40, actualVotingRightsPercentage = 66.7.~  §10.2.0* 40% fails D1, but 66.7% of voting rights is evidenced, so D2 applies - dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D2 majority voting rights], dominationOwnership = 0 (no majority holding), dominationVotingRights = 66.7 (§10.2.1* the direct voting figure the determination rests on).~  Both percentages are stated and they differ, so ownershipVotingMismatch = TRUE.~  Example*~  A shareholder agreement gives Parent Corp the right to appoint board majority.~  - Extract the contractual control right into controlRights, and take §10.2.0 D3* dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D3 right to appoint / remove board majority], dominationOwnership = 0 and dominationVotingRights = 0 (the basis is a control right, not a percentage - §10.2.1), controlBasedUBOAssessmentRequired = TRUE.~  - The control-based qualification is then MET, not merely available* §12.2.1 criterion 3 for a Natural Person, §12.4 for a Non-Natural Person. See §20 example E for the full worked record.~  </rule>~~  <rule id="11" priority="HIGH" name="ENTITY-TYPE SPECIFIC OWNERSHIP LOGIC">~  11.1 Private / Regulated / Branch / FinTech / MSB~  Apply full layer-by-layer extraction unless streamlined treatment is explicitly permitted.~  Continue ownership extraction through all ownership layers until a valid endpoint permitted by applicable Global KOS and Local Addenda is reached.~  A valid endpoint may include a Natural Person UBO, Listed Entity, Government Entity / SOE, or other exempt entity where the applicable stop rule is evidenced and permitted.~  Upon reaching a valid endpoint, terminate ownership extraction beyond that endpoint and do not continue shareholder, ownership, or control analysis unless an applicable local rule, documented exception, or regulatory instruction requires continued review.~  11.1.1 Where no natural person is identified at the applicable ownership threshold and Notional UBO fallback is required*~  - Identify the Senior Most CSM (if can be identified via Designation ONLY) in accordance with applicable Global KOS and Local Addenda.~  - DO NOT classify the individual as Notional UBO.~  - Emit QA Flag* NOTIONAL_UBO_ASSESSMENT_REQUIRED~  - Record the basis for the Notional UBO determin','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
