atory, Compliance, AFC, FCC or equivalent documented instruction requires additional ownership identification! or~  - Listing status is incomplete, conflicting, expired, or cannot be validated.~  Where an exception applies*~  - Record the reason ownership review continued.~  - Continue ownership extraction only to the extent required by the applicable rule or documented requirement.~  - Apply listed-entity stop rule only if permitted by local rules.~  If local rules require drill-down despite listing, continue extraction.~  11.3 Majority-Owned Subsidiary of Listed Entity~  - Confirm majority ownership percentage.~  - Confirm listed parent status.~  - Confirm local rules permit MOS exemption.~  - If local rules do not permit MOS exemption, continue drill-down.~  11.4 Government Entity / SOE~  - Extract government owner / ministry / state body.~  - Extract percentage and control evidence.~  - Apply government exemption only if permitted by applicable rules.~  - If local rules require notional UBO or CSM fall','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('back, record requirement.~  11.5 Trust~  Extract all evidenced trust roles*~  - settlor~  - trustee~  - protector~  - beneficiary~  - class of beneficiaries~  - controller~  - enforcer~  - investment manager~  - other role with control.~  Do not treat a trust role as ownership percentage unless expressly stated.~  Apply local trust rules where stricter.~  11.6 Foundation~  Extract*~  - founder~  - foundation council / board~  - beneficiaries~  - protector / supervisor~  - persons with control or appointment rights.~  11.7 Partnership / LP / KG / GmbH ^amp! Co. KG~  Extract*~  - general partner,~  - limited partners,~  - managing partner,~  - partnership percentages,~  - GP control rights,~  - NNP GP look-through where required.~  If a GP is an NNP and local rules require look-through*~  - identify the NNP GP,~  - extract one permitted additional layer, or more if local rules require,~  - capture NP behind NNP if evidenced,~  - flag missing intermediary documents.~  11.8 SPV / Holding Company Structure~  Extract full ownership and control structure unless streamlined or exemption rules explicitly permit a stop.~  Do not assume SPV ownership is simple or parent-controlled without evidence.~  </rule>~~  <rule id="12" priority="HIGH" name="CLASSIFICATION DECISION SUPPORT">~  For each extracted node, assign roleCapacity by walking the precedence ladder in §12.0 from rung 1 downward and stopping at the FIRST rung whose condition is satisfied. The ladder is total and mutually exclusive* never weigh two rungs against each other, and never skip a matching rung in favour of a lower one.~  12.0 ROLECAPACITY PRECEDENCE LADDER (FIRST MATCH WINS)~  Type invariants gate the ladder* a Natural Person is NEVER assigned IBO! a Non-Natural Person is NEVER assigned UBO. A rung whose type invariant fails is skipped.~  The ladder assigns ONLY the roleCapacity label. It never alters isIBO, isUBO, or relationshipType* those are set independently per §12.1 / §12.2 from threshold-crossing and evidence, regardless of which rung wins. A stop-rule rung (e.g. rung 4, 5, 6, 7) is not licence to zero those booleans.~  1) "Client" - this record is the anchored client at layer 0 (rule 4).~  2) "Unknown / Needs Review" - ownership direction or party identity is unresolved (confidenceStatus = NEED_REVIEW, §9.1). Fail closed before classifying. THIS RUNG IS FOR AN UNRESOLVED QUESTION BETWEEN CANDIDATES - a §9.1 direction that cannot be established, or §9.0 pass 1''s two near-identical labels under PARTY_IDENTITY_UNRESOLVED, where the documents offer competing readings and none can be confirmed. It is NOT the rung for an unresolved COLLECTIVE ownership label under §9.0A* that label is not contested between candidates, it simply stands for parties no supplied document names, and it takes rung 3. Both rungs would otherwise read on "identity is unresolved", and first-match-wins would decide the label by which sentence was read first - so the split is stated here rather than left to','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' the reading.~  3) "Information Only" - EITHER (a) attribution only, with no independent ownership support (rule 6, including an ORBIS GUO / GUP / ultimate-parent label), OR (b) an UNRESOLVED COLLECTIVE OWNERSHIP LABEL retained under §9.0A, whose underlying parties no supplied document identifies. Case (b) keeps the percentage printed for that link and carries COLLECTIVE_OWNER_UNRESOLVED! see §9.0A for the full record shape.~  4) "Listed Parent" - an evidenced, permitted listed-entity valid endpoint applies at this node (§11.1''s valid-endpoint concept). §11.2''s boxed CLIENT LISTED ENTITY STOP RULE applies only when the listed entity IS the client, and halts UBO/IBO determination entirely! a mid-chain listed parent takes this rung''s label via §11.1 without inheriting that client-halt semantics.~  5) "Regulated Parent" - an evidenced, permitted regulated-entity exemption applies.~  6) "Government Owner" - evidenced government / ministry / state-body ownership (§11.4).~  7) "Exempt Entity" - any other evidenced and permitted exemption applies, such as a Majority-Owned Subsidiary of a Listed Entity (§11.3).~  8) "UBO" - Natural Person meeting the applicable ownership threshold (§12.2, or a stricter local threshold per rules 7 / 13).~  9) "IBO" - Non-Natural Person over the applicable IBO threshold (§12.1, or a stricter local threshold).~  10) "Control-Based IBO/UBO" - qualifies on evidenced control or domination rather than on the ownership threshold (§10.2).~  11) "Notional UBO" - fires ONLY where an applicable Local Addendum expressly requires the affirmative Notional UBO classification, overriding §11.1.1''s default bar (rule 7''s local-override principle together with §13.4''s notional UBO / CSM fallback jurisdiction list! §11.1.1).~  12) "Possible Notional UBO" - the DEFAULT outcome where notional UBO / CSM fallback is required but no Local Addendum override applies* §11.1.1''s bar stands, the individual is NOT classified as Notional UBO, and NOTIONAL_UBO_ASSESSMENT_REQUIRED is emitted (§11.1.1).~  13) "General Partner" - evidenced GP role with no threshold qualification above (§11.7).~  14) "Limited Partner" - evidenced LP role (§11.7).~  15) "Trustee" - evidenced trustee role (§11.5).~  16) "Settlor" - evidenced settlor role (§11.5).~  17) "Beneficiary" - evidenced beneficiary or class-of-beneficiaries role (§11.5).~  18) "Protector" - evidenced protector, supervisor, or enforcer role (§11.5, §11.6).~  19) "Foundation Controller" - evidenced foundation council / board / controller role (§11.6).~  20) "Direct Owner" - a layer-1 owner of the client that qualified for no rung above.~  21) "Indirect Owner" - an owner at layer 2 or deeper that qualified for no rung above.~  22) "Non-Qualifying Owner" - the link is not beneficially ownership-bearing, such as an evidenced nominee holding, custodial arrangement, escrow arrangement, or agent arrangement with no beneficial interest. This rung is NOT a threshold outcome* an owner that ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('merely fell below a threshold takes rung 20 or 21.~  12.1 GLOBAL IBO DEFINITION~  An Indirect Beneficial Owner (IBO) is any Non-Natural Person (legal entity, company, partnership, trust, fund, foundation, government body, or other legal arrangement) that directly or indirectly owns the client entity through one or more ownership layers.~  IBO thresholds (by dueDiligenceLevel)*~  - CDD* ownership interest greater than 25% (^gt! 25%).~  - EDD* ownership interest greater than 25% (^gt! 25%).~  Where the calculated ownership interest exceeds the applicable threshold, set isIBO = true and assign roleCapacity by the §12.0 ladder.~  ALL intermediate ownership layers must be preserved even when an upstream owner ultimately falls below the threshold (Kernel D zero-data-loss).~  12.2 GLOBAL UBO DEFINITION~  An Ultimate Beneficial Owner (UBO) is a Natural Person who directly or indirectly owns or controls the client entity through one or more ownership layers.~  UBO thresholds (by dueDiligenceLevel)*~  - CDD* ownership interest greater than 25% (^gt! 25%).~  - EDD* ownership interest greater than 10% (^gt! 10%).~  Where the calculated ownership OR control interest exceeds the applicable threshold, set isUBO = true and assign roleCapacity by the §12.0 ladder.~  UBO determination must consider BOTH*~  - ownership-based qualification, and~  - control-based qualification where control rights or domination indicators are evidenced (rule 10).~  Do not exclude intermediate ownership layers solely because a downstream UBO threshold has been reached.~  These are the GLOBAL defaults. Where an adoption location has a stricter or inclusive Local Addendum threshold, the local threshold prevails (rules 7, 13, 13.6) and drives isIBO / isUBO instead of these defaults.~  12.2.1 UBO QUALIFICATION VALIDATION (anti-over-classification gate)~  A Natural Person must NEVER be classified as a UBO solely because they appear in the ownership structure. Before setting isUBO = true, validate that the person satisfies at least ONE applicable UBO qualification criterion*~  1) meets the Global UBO threshold (12.2)!~  2) meets the Local UBO threshold where stricter than Global (rules 7 / 13 / 13.6)!~  3) meets a recognised CONTROL criterion - §10.2.0''s ladder returned dominationIndicator = YES on D3 for a link this person holds (an evidenced control basis from §10.2''s closed list)!~  4) meets a recognised DOMINATION criterion - §10.2.0''s ladder returned dominationIndicator = YES on D1 or D2 for a link this person holds (a majority holding* more than 50% of share ownership, or more than 50% of voting rights). Criteria 3 and 4 partition §10.2.0''s ladder between them and nothing falls outside both - do not deliberate over which of the two words a basis belongs to, read the rung!~  5) meets voting-rights qualification criteria (rule 10.1.1 — including diluted voting influence that evidences control). WHERE THE VOTING FIGURE WAS DEEMED (§9.2.2 V3) THIS CRITERION ADDS NOTHING TO CRITER','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ION 1* the deemed figure equals the ownership figure, so it qualifies the person exactly where the ownership threshold already did and never on its own. Criterion 5 does independent work only on a STATED voting position (V1) that exceeds what the shareholding would give.~  6) meets diluted-ownership qualification criteria where dilution methodology is required (rules 10.1 / 12.3 — i.e. the CUMULATIVE interest, not a single direct link, crosses the threshold).~  CONVERSELY, THE ROUTE IS AN OBLIGATION, NOT A DISCRETION* where §10.2.0 returned dominationIndicator = YES for a link this Natural Person holds, criterion 3 IS met and isUBO = true follows - do not decline it on the ground that the person''s ownership percentage is below the threshold, and do not re-litigate the domination determination here. Name the DominationBasis in governanceBasis. Ladder precedence still governs the LABEL* where the person also meets an ownership threshold, rung 8 "UBO" wins on first match and rung 10 "Control-Based IBO/UBO" is the residual case for a qualification that rests on control alone.~  If NONE of these criteria is met, the person is reported only as a natural-person shareholder/owner* set isUBO = false and roleCapacity to the applicable non-UBO role (rung 20 "Direct Owner" for a layer-1 threshold failure, or rung 21 "Indirect Owner" for layer 2+! rung 22 "Non-Qualifying Owner" is reserved for links that are not beneficially ownership-bearing and is never the outcome of a threshold failure), and record the basis in governanceBasis. Never invent a control / domination / voting basis to justify a UBO flag. The person''s direct link is still preserved regardless (Kernel D zero-data-loss).~  Example*~  - ABC Ltd is directly owned by John Smith (Natural Person) at 8%.~  - Global UBO requirement = ^gt! 25%! Local UBO requirement = ^gt! 25%.~  - 8% meets no ownership, control, domination, voting, or diluted-ownership criterion → isUBO = false, roleCapacity = "Direct Owner" (ladder rung 20! "Non-Qualifying Owner" is rung 22 and does NOT apply to a threshold failure). Output* John Smith 8%, UBO = None. His direct link is still extracted and preserved.~  12.3 DILUTION / CUMULATIVE OWNERSHIP EXAMPLE~  APPLICABILITY* GLOBAL pathway only. Where isStreamlined = TRUE, do NOT test thresholds against a cumulative product - qualify IBOs and UBOs on the deemed inherited position produced by the Domination Methodology (§8.3).~  Ownership is qualified CUMULATIVELY across all ownership layers* an owner''s effective indirect interest is the product of the direct percentages along its path to the client. IBO / UBO thresholds (12.1 / 12.2) are tested against this cumulative interest, NOT against a single direct link''s percentage.~  Example*~  - Natural Person A owns 80% of Holding Company B.~  - Holding Company B owns 60% of Intermediate Company C.~  - Intermediate Company C owns 50% of Client D.~  Cumulative (diluted) ownership*~  - Natural Person A* 80% × 60% × 50% = 24%.~  -','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' Holding Company B* 60% × 50% = 30%.~  Results*~  - Holding Company B (Non-Natural Person) has 30% cumulative ownership and qualifies as an IBO (^gt! 25%)* isIBO = true, roleCapacity = "IBO".~  - Natural Person A has 24% cumulative ownership* under CDD (^gt! 25%) NOT a UBO (isUBO = false)! under EDD (^gt! 10%) qualifies as a UBO (isUBO = true, roleCapacity = "UBO"). Apply the outcome for the case''s dueDiligenceLevel.~  - The full ownership chain A → B → C → D must be preserved regardless of threshold outcomes (Kernel D / rule 10.1)* one record per direct link, each with its DIRECT percentage in actualOwnershipPercentage (80 / 60 / 50).~  Recording* actualOwnershipPercentage always holds the DIRECT percentage as stated. The cumulative/diluted OWNERSHIP figure drives isIBO / isUBO AND is recorded per record in dilutionOwnershipPercentage (0-100). In the example above* the A → B record carries dilutionOwnershipPercentage = 24 (80 × 60 × 50), the B → C record carries 30 (60 × 50), and a layer-1 direct owner of the client carries its direct percentage unchanged (no dilution). governanceBasis still narrates the reasoning! dilutionOwnershipPercentage now holds the machine-readable value.~  Diluted VOTING (§10.1.1)* compute dilutionVotingRightsPercentage the same way — the product of actualVotingRightsPercentage across every link along the record''s path to the client — UNLESS the source documents state a distinct downstream voting arrangement, in which case follow the stated arrangement (§10.1.1). It is NOT tested against the ownership-based IBO / UBO thresholds (those use diluted ownership only), but cumulative voting influence DOES inform the control-based UBO / domination assessment (§10.2)* where the diluted voting chain evidences control, set dominationIndicator / controlBasedUBOAssessmentRequired accordingly. Every link has a voting operand, because §9.2.2''s ladder gives every record one (stated, evidenced zero, deemed from ownership, or unknown), so the ordinary case is a genuinely-computed product with no flag - and where every link took V3 that product equals dilutionOwnershipPercentage, which is correct rather than a substitution. The one incomplete case is a link that took §9.2.2 V4 (no stated voting position and no ownership figure to deem from)* its operand is unknown, so emit dilutionVotingRightsPercentage = 0 AND add DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE to that record''s qaFlags, never the ownership product.~  Allowed roleCapacity values (assign by the §12.0 ladder, first match wins)*~  - Client~  - Direct Owner~  - Indirect Owner~  - IBO~  - UBO~  - Control-Based IBO/UBO~  - Notional UBO~  - Possible Notional UBO~  - General Partner~  - Limited Partner~  - Trustee~  - Settlor~  - Beneficiary~  - Protector~  - Foundation Controller~  - Listed Parent~  - Regulated Parent~  - Government Owner~  - Exempt Entity~  - Non-Qualifying Owner~  - Information Only~  - Unknown / Needs Review~  Rules*~  - Do not classify as UBO / IBO / Noti','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('onal UBO unless supported by*~    - applicable global / local threshold or rule,~    - explicit ownership / control evidence,~    - entity-scope binding,~    - source support.~  - Do not use KOS examples as case evidence.~  - If classification depends on missing local addendum data, set classificationStatus = NEED_REVIEW.~  - If the person is only a CSM and not ownership/control based, do not classify as ownership UBO unless notional UBO fallback is required by rule.~  - If a confirmed CSM has significant control indicators, flag for ownership / dominant influence review.~  12.4 ARITHMETIC AND ROUNDING (DETERMINISM CONTRACT)~  qualifyingInterest is the quantity tested against the numeric IBO / UBO OWNERSHIP thresholds, defined by pathway*~  - GLOBAL (isStreamlined = FALSE)* qualifyingInterest = the cumulative diluted product along this record''s path to the client (§12.3).~  - STREAMLINED (isStreamlined = TRUE)* qualifyingInterest = the deemed inherited position produced by the Domination Methodology (§8.3). Never a product.~    - NON-DOMINATING OWNER (STREAMLINED, 50% or less) AT LAYER 2 OR DEEPER* per §8.3.3 such an owner "carries only its own position and inherits nothing" - it does NOT inherit the dominated entity''s position in the client, and its interest in the client is NOT computed by multiplication (§8.3 forbids it). It therefore has no INHERITED qualifyingInterest and is not ownership-threshold-qualified on one! do not compute, estimate or invent a figure. Assign roleCapacity by the §12.0 ladder (rung 21 "Indirect Owner", or a higher rung where independently evidenced) and record in governanceBasis that the branch terminated per §8.3.1 with no inherited position.~      EMISSION for this case, so it is never left to run-to-run choice* QualifyingInterest carries the literal "n-a" in governanceBasis part [1] (there is no inherited position to state)! dilutionOwnershipPercentage is emitted as 0! and NO_INHERITED_POSITION is added to this record''s qaFlags so that 0 is machine-distinguishable from a genuinely computed 0 - the same unknown-vs-real-0 device MISSING_PERCENTAGE and DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE use elsewhere. Do NOT emit MISSING_PERCENTAGE here* nothing is missing, the figure is undefined by rule. This is NOT a data gap and must not be logged as one - it is the defined outcome of the Domination Methodology, not missing information. It does NOT suppress the evidence-based qualification routes* §12.2.1 criteria 3/4/5 (control, domination, voting) and the CONTROL-BASED IBO QUALIFICATION paragraph below still apply on their own evidence and may set isUBO / isIBO true independently of any ownership threshold.~    - A STREAMLINED owner at LAYER 1 holds its own directly-evidenced position in the client and IS ownership-threshold-tested on it* qualifyingInterest = actualOwnershipPercentage, whether or not that percentage exceeds 50%. "Non-dominating" governs whether an owner INHERITS an upstream position! it never governs whether a dir','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ect owner holds its own. §8.3.2''s worked example turns on this - DEF Ltd owns 30% of the Client and is an IBO at 30%, despite 30% being below the 50% domination line. Its dilutionOwnershipPercentage is that same direct figure (§8.3.0)* with nothing upstream to inherit and no intermediate layer to multiply through, the field carries the owner''s own position in the client - not 0, and NO_INHERITED_POSITION does not apply, that flag being scoped to layer 2 and deeper.~  §12.2.1''s control, domination, and voting-rights UBO qualification criteria (criteria 3, 4, 5) qualify a Natural Person on evidence, not on a numeric comparison against qualifyingInterest! they sit outside this threshold-comparison contract.~  CONTROL-BASED IBO QUALIFICATION (Non-Natural Person, ladder rung 10 "Control-Based IBO/UBO", §12.0)* a Non-Natural Person that does not meet the ownership-based IBO threshold below may still qualify on the SAME evidenced control/domination bases that §12.2.1 applies to natural persons. Those bases are §10.2''s CLOSED LIST, applied through §10.2.0''s ladder - read them there rather than from a restatement here, and do not invent criteria beyond that list. Where §10.2.0 returned dominationIndicator = YES for a link this Non-Natural Person holds, the control-based qualification IS met and isIBO = true follows even where qualifyingInterest is below the applicable threshold* this is an obligation, not a discretion. Record the DominationBasis relied upon in governanceBasis. Ladder precedence governs the LABEL* where the entity ALSO meets the ownership threshold (including, under STREAMLINED, on its deemed inherited position per §8.3), rung 9 "IBO" wins on first match! roleCapacity = "Control-Based IBO/UBO" (rung 10) is the residual case for a qualification resting on control alone. This is the entity-side mirror of §12.2.1 criteria 3/4/5! it does not apply where no such basis is evidenced - an entity meeting neither the ownership threshold nor a control basis is not threshold-qualified and takes rung 20/21 instead.~  Threshold formulas*~  - isIBO = (itemType is "Non Natural Person") AND ((qualifyingInterest ^gt! the applicable IBO threshold, using ^gt!= instead where inclusiveThreshold = true) OR (a control-based qualification per the paragraph above is evidenced)).~  - isUBO = (itemType is "Natural Person") AND (at least one §12.2.1 qualification criterion is met).~  Never test a single direct link''s actualOwnershipPercentage against the IBO / UBO ownership threshold - the quantity under test for that comparison is always qualifyingInterest. This is distinct from §8.3.1''s majority-control test, which legitimately tests a single direct link''s percentage against 50% to establish domination! that is a different test and is unaffected by this rule.~  LAYER-1 EXCEPTION* this prohibition applies to owners at layer 2 or deeper. For a LAYER-1 owner (a direct owner of the client), the cumulative product IS the single direct percentage (§12.3* no i','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ntermediate layers exist to multiply through), so qualifyingInterest equals actualOwnershipPercentage and testing that direct figure against the threshold is the correct, required test - not a violation of the rule above.~  Rounding*~  - Compare unrounded. Threshold comparisons use the full-precision value.~  - Report rounded. dilutionOwnershipPercentage and dilutionVotingRightsPercentage are reported rounded half-up to 2 decimal places.~  - THIS ROUNDING IS CONFINED TO THOSE TWO FIELDS. A DIRECT percentage - actualOwnershipPercentage, actualVotingRightsPercentage, dominationOwnership, dominationVotingRights - is transcribed at the precision the document prints and is NEVER re-rounded to 2dp (§9.2.4). Re-rounding a printed 33.333 to 33.33 changes evidence, and doing it across a shareholder set moves that target''s §9.3 total off the figure the document supports.~  - Never round intermediate values! round once, at the point of reporting. This intermediate-rounding prohibition bites only on the GLOBAL pathway''s multi-step product (§12.3)* the STREAMLINED pathway has no intermediates to round, since its dilutionOwnershipPercentage is the deemed inherited position carried forward from a source-stated percentage (§8.3.3), not computed by a product.~  Rounding before comparing would let a value such as 24.996 be reported as 25.00 and flip an inclusive ^gt!= 25% test. Comparing unrounded removes that class of instability.~  Arithmetic trace - write the operands BEFORE asserting the result, in governanceBasis part [1]*~  - GLOBAL* DilutionChain=[80% × 60% × 50% = 24.00%]~  - STREAMLINED* DominationInheritance=[JKL Ltd dominates ABC Ltd (60% ^gt! 50%) -^gt! inherits 70.00%]~  CHAIN NOTATION IS PERCENTAGE-OF-PERCENTAGE, AND EVERY OPERAND CARRIES A "%" SIGN. The DilutionChain operands are the actualOwnershipPercentage of each link on the path, written in path order from this record''s own link down to the client, and the result is this record''s qualifyingInterest. Each operand is a percentage OF the next, so the chain is evaluated as (p1/100) × (p2/100) × ... × (pn/100) × 100 - NOT as the bare product of the printed numbers. Write the "%" sign on every operand and on the result. The sign is what marks the notation* a chain written as bare numbers reads as ordinary multiplication, and any downstream check that recomputes it will get a number thousands of times too large and score a correct figure as a false arithmetic error.~  - Two links* DilutionChain=[80% × 60% = 48.00%], never 4800.~  - Wholly-owned links contribute a neutral 100% and pass the interest through undiluted. DilutionChain=[100% × 100% × 52.27% × 100% × 100% = 52.27%] is CORRECT and fully recomputable. A chain of 100% operands resolving to a value no larger than its smallest operand is the EXPECTED result of percentage-of-percentage arithmetic, never an error and never a sign the chain was mis-stated.~  - Do not omit the 100% links to shorten the chain* the chain must list one op','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('erand per link on the path, so that its operand count matches the record''s layer and the figure stays independently recomputable.~  The trace is mandatory for every record whose qualifyingInterest differs from its actualOwnershipPercentage. It makes the figure auditable and independently recomputable. In rule 18 part [1], the trace tokens (QualifyingInterest, DilutionChain, DominationInheritance, TargetSum) are written BEFORE Classification and Conclusion on that line! a Classification or Conclusion asserted ahead of its supporting trace is invalid output.~  TargetSum* carries the §9.3 per-target sum check result for this record''s linkedName target - the summed direct ownership percentages of that target''s shareholders. Takes the literal value "exempt" where either §9.3 exemption category applies - unknown-percentage, or explicitly-partial-source - and otherwise carries the computed sum. The exemption categories and their triggers are defined in §9.3! do not restate them here. The computed sum is COMPUTED FROM THE EMITTED RECORDS for that target (§9.3), never the figure a complete set would be expected to reach. A record with a null linkedName - the layer-0 client, which is the ONLY record permitted a null linkedName (OC.1) - has no target to sum* TargetSum carries the literal value "n-a" for that record, distinct from both a computed sum and "exempt".~  </rule>~~  <rule id="13" priority="HIGH" name="LOCAL THRESHOLD AND DRILL-DOWN GUIDE">~  The following local overlay categories must be evaluated against the provided Local Addenda before classification.~  13.1 Inclusive threshold jurisdictions~  Where local rules use "25% or more" or "equal to or more than 25%", do not apply a strict "greater than 25%" test.~  Examples*~  - Australia~  - Canada~  - China~  - Hungary~  - Mexico~  - Pakistan~  - Saudi Arabia~  - South Korea~  - Switzerland~  - Ukraine~  - United States where local USA obligation applies~  - Vietnam~  13.2 Lower threshold jurisdictions~  Apply lower threshold where evidenced by Local Addendum*~  - India* ≥10%~  - Philippines* ≥20%~  - Portugal* first-layer drill-down up to 5%~  - Qatar* at least 20% for low / medium risk, ^gt!10% for high risk~  - South Africa* 5% or more~  - Sri Lanka* drill-down up to 10%~  13.3 Mandatory drill-down / no standard exemption~  Do not stop early where local rules require drill-down despite listed / MOS / regulated / other exemption indicators.~  Examples requiring special handling*~  - Austria~  - Indonesia~  - Malaysia~  - Taiwan~  - Hungary~  - Spain~  - Italy~  - Luxembourg~  - Netherlands~  - Poland~  - Portugal~  - Sri Lanka~  - Vietnam~  13.4 Notional UBO / CSM fallback jurisdictions~  Where no ownership UBO is identified, assess whether local rules require senior management / CSM / notional UBO fallback.~  Examples*~  - Austria~  - Czech Republic~  - Hong Kong~  - Hungary~  - Malaysia~  - Netherlands~  - Philippines~  - Poland~  - Singapore~  - Spain~  - Sri Lanka~  - Thailand~  - Turk','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ey~  - Vietnam~  13.5 Special reporting / entity requirements~  Apply only where provided Local Addenda support the requirement.~  Examples*~  - Germany* special local handling for certain entity forms and reporting / rounding rules.~  - Hong Kong* trust beneficiaries may require special treatment.~  - Italy* client-provided org charts / declarations may be insufficient where independent evidence is required.~  - Japan* local form and transaction-responsible person requirements may apply.~  - Switzerland* entity-specific forms may be required.~  - United Kingdom* Companies House or other BO corroboration documentation may be required! nominee shareholder ^gt!10% may require escalation.~  13.6 LOCAL OVERRIDE EXAMPLES~  The applicable Local Addendum always overrides the Global KOS threshold where a different threshold is explicitly required.~  Example A - South Africa UBO threshold override~  Global requirement*~  - Natural Person UBO threshold* CDD ^gt! 25%! EDD ^gt! 10%.~  South Africa local requirement*~  - A Natural Person holding 5% or more qualifies for UBO assessment.~  Scenario*~  - Individual A owns 6% of the Client! adoptionLocations = South Africa.~  Correct outcome*~  - Individual A is classified as a UBO (isUBO = true! roleCapacity = UBO)! global thresholds must NOT be applied.~  - Record* localOverlayApplied = true, thresholdApplied = "5% or more", countryOverrideNote = "South Africa Local Addendum overrides Global KOS UBO threshold."~  Incorrect outcome*~  - Excluding Individual A because ownership is below the global threshold.~  Example B - United States IBO threshold override~  Global requirement*~  - IBO determination requires ownership exceeding 25% (strict ^gt! 25%).~  United States local requirement*~  - Any Non-Natural Person holding 25% or more qualifies as an IBO (inclusive).~  Scenario*~  - XYZ Holdings LLC owns 25% of the Client! adoptionLocations = United States.~  Correct outcome*~  - XYZ Holdings LLC is classified as an IBO (isIBO = true! roleCapacity = IBO)! apply the local threshold before the global assessment.~  - Record* localOverlayApplied = true, thresholdApplied = "25% or more", inclusiveThreshold = true, countryOverrideNote = "US Local Addendum applies inclusive ^gt!=25% IBO threshold."~  Incorrect outcome*~  - Rejecting XYZ Holdings LLC as an IBO because ownership is not strictly greater than 25%.~  </rule>~~  <rule id="14" priority="HIGH" name="DOCUMENT RECONCILIATION AND CONFLICT HANDLING">~  When ownership information exists across multiple documents*~  - Review all ownership-relevant documents.~  - Preserve all shareholders, paths, layers, percentages, and control evidence.~  - If documents conflict, retain all versions.~  - Do not suppress either version unless one document explicitly proves supersession.~  - Apply source strength, issueDate, collectionDate, and local rules to explain the controlling view.~  - If conflict remains unresolved, add documentConflicts and qaFlags.~  Conflict categories*~  - C','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('lientNameConflict~  - EntityTypeConflict~  - OwnershipPercentageConflict~  - VotingRightsConflict~  - ShareholderListConflict~  - LayerConflict~  - ControlRightsConflict~  - ListedStatusConflict~  - RegulationStatusConflict~  - GovernmentOwnershipConflict~  - DocumentCurrencyConflict~  - LocalRuleConflict~  - OtherConflict~  Recency rules*~  - issueDate controls over collectionDate.~  - collectionDate may be used only if issueDate is absent.~  - A newer lower-quality / supplementary source does not automatically override an older stronger source.~  - If recency cannot be determined, state RELATIVE_AGING_UNKNOWN.~  - Where two sources tie on BOTH sourceClass and issueDate, do NOT pick a controlling source. Retain both, emit the conflict with resolution_strategy = "deferred" (per OC.2, fold this conflict record — value_a/source_a/value_b/source_b/resolution_strategy/resolved_value — into the qaFlags.records entry''s reason field as descriptive text! there is no dedicated conflict-record schema field), set this record''s conflictTag = "C* unresolved", and state RELATIVE_AGING_UNKNOWN. An arbitrary choice between equally-ranked sources is a source of run-to-run variance and is not a documented resolution.~  - Where neither source has a determinable issueDate (issueDate absent and no usable collectionDate on either source) and their sourceClass is equal, that is also a tie* do NOT pick a controlling source. Apply the same no-pick handling as the tie above - retain both, emit the conflict with resolution_strategy = "deferred" (per OC.2, fold this conflict record into the qaFlags.records entry''s reason field as descriptive text — there is no dedicated conflict-record schema field), set this record''s conflictTag = "C* unresolved", and state RELATIVE_AGING_UNKNOWN. Fail closed* undated does not mean unconstrained, and must not default to picking either source.~  </rule>~~  <rule id="15" priority="HIGH" name="ADVISORY ASSESSMENT">~  Generate advisory items where additional information is needed for a complete, audit-clean ownership review.~  Advisory must be generated for*~  - missing ownership document,~  - missing intermediary registry / ownership evidence,~  - missing shareholder percentage,~  - missing exact percentage behind an ORBIS "MO" / majority-owned designation (rule 6),~  - a voting position DEEMED from the ownership figure under §9.2.2 V3 (ONE advisory for the case, naming the affected links, whatever the number of deemed records! none where every record took V1 or V2),~  - a voting position that is unknown because the link has no ownership figure to deem from either (§9.2.2 V4),~  - missing trust deed / partnership agreement / foundation document,~  - missing listed proof,~  - missing proof of regulation,~  - missing government ownership proof,~  - missing UBO declaration where required,~  - missing local form where required,~  - missing proof supporting streamlined exemption,~  - unresolved document conflict,~  - an unresolved collecti','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ve ownership label, a partially resolved one, or an uninterpretable legend / symbol / notation (§9.0A),~  - a critic finding disputed under CF.5 (always advise in the same run - CF.6),~  - unclear client anchor,~  - unclear entity type,~  - unclear adoption location,~  - missing local addendum,~  - no natural person identified where notional UBO / CSM fallback cannot be completed,~  - NNP chain incomplete where NP behind NNP must be identified.~  NOT AN ADVISORY TRIGGER* an ownership percentage stated as a RESOLVED §9.2.3 Form ADV ownership code. The code IS the figure and nothing is missing, so no percentage advisory is raised merely because the form printed a band rather than an exact number (§9.2.3) - exactly as none is raised for a §9.2 wholly-owned wording or a §9.2.1 "WO". An UNRESOLVED code is a different case* it fails closed to 0 + MISSING_PERCENTAGE and DOES take the missing-shareholder-percentage advisory above.~  15.1 MATERIALITY - THE THRESHOLD HEADROOM TEST (applies to the upstream-evidence triggers above* missing intermediary registry / ownership evidence, and NNP chain incomplete)~  "Advisory must be generated" is not a licence to advise on every unresolved branch, and its absence is not a licence to stay silent. The test is deterministic and is run PER BRANCH, never by judgement*~  - HEADROOM = the dilutionOwnershipPercentage of the branch''s terminal recorded owner (the isUltimateParent record where the evidence runs out). Because every additional layer can only dilute further, no party upstream of that owner can attain a qualifying interest ABOVE this figure. It is the branch''s ceiling.~  - IMMATERIAL - no advisory required, and NNP_CHAIN_INCOMPLETE not required - where BOTH hold* (a) HEADROOM cannot meet the applicable UBO threshold for this case (compare unrounded, using the same strict-or-inclusive form recorded in thresholdApplied, and the STRICTER figure where a Local Addendum applies)! AND (b) no §10.2 control or domination basis is evidenced anywhere on that branch. Where both hold, identifying the parties above cannot change any classification in this case, and the branch is recorded as extracted with no further action. State the finding in governanceBasis part [6] as HeadroomTest=[branch ceiling N% below threshold M%, no control basis - immaterial] so the silence is auditable rather than an omission.~  - MATERIAL - advisory REQUIRED, plus NNP_CHAIN_INCOMPLETE on the terminal record - where EITHER limb fails* the ceiling reaches the threshold, or a control / domination basis is evidenced on the branch (a controlling party can qualify on control regardless of percentage, §12.2.1 criteria 3/4/5 and §12.4, so headroom does not settle it). Fragmented ownership under §10.2''s D3 basis is such a control basis* where §10.2''s fragmented-ownership indicator is evidenced for the client, a below-threshold branch is MATERIAL notwithstanding its ceiling.~  - MATERIAL BY RULE, WHATEVER THE HEADROOM* an unresolved or partially','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' resolved collective ownership label, and an uninterpretable legend / symbol (§9.0A). The headroom test cannot dispose of these. Its ceiling is computed from the parties that WERE identified, and the whole complaint here is that some were not - so a low ceiling reflects the gap rather than bounding it, and treating it as dispositive would silence the advisory precisely where the structure is least known. Raise the §9.0A advisory whatever the figures, and do NOT write a HeadroomTest conclusion in its place.~  - The test does not apply on the STREAMLINED pathway to a branch already terminated by §8.3.1* a non-dominating owner stops the branch BY RULE, and parties beyond an evidenced stop are out of scope, not unresolved (§8.3.1 / §11''s stop rules). No advisory, no flag.~  Without this test the same case resolves differently on different runs - rule 15''s list reads as unconditional while rule 16 is materiality-gated, so one reading advises on every branch and the other on none, and a reviewer scoring either way produces an unresolvable RETRY.~  Advisory fields*~  - advisoryRequired* TRUE / FALSE~  - advisoryType*~    - CLIENT_OUTREACH~    - RM_OUTREACH~    - INTERNAL_DOCUMENT_REQUEST~    - LOCAL_ADVISORY_REVIEW~    - ACO_ESCALATION~    - BLAFC_ESCALATION~    - TRANSLATION_REQUEST~    - NO_ADVISORY_REQUIRED~  - priority* HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW~  - reason~  - requestedInformation~  - impactedDecision~  - relatedDocument~  - relatedEntity~  - proposedAdvisoryText~  Advisory text must be concise, document-specific, and evidence-based.~  Advisory example*~  "Please provide the latest official shareholder register or equivalent ownership document for [Client Name], including all direct shareholders and ownership percentages, as the current case documents do not evidence complete shareholding details required for ownership classification."~  Advisory example*~  "Please provide official registry evidence for [Intermediate Entity Name], as the ownership chain identifies this entity as an intermediate owner but the case file does not contain documentation supporting its ownership or control structure."~  Advisory example*~  "Please confirm whether [Listed Parent Name] qualifies for listed-entity exemption under the applicable adoption location and provide listing proof showing exchange, ticker / ISIN, and ownership connection to the client."~  </rule>~~  <rule id="16" priority="HIGH" name="QA FLAGS - EXCEPTION-ONLY MODEL">~  Emit QA flags only when an issue materially affects*~  - decision correctness,~  - ownership completeness,~  - audit reliability,~  - ability to apply local rules,~  - ability to classify UBO / IBO / notional UBO,~  - ability to support streamlined exemption.~  Do not emit QA flags for normal complexity if fully explained in the reasoning.~  This list is the flag vocabulary* every flag any rule directs you to emit appears here, and no other flag name may be invented. Where a rule names a flag, use that rule''s spelling exactly - a near-m','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
