he local rules are simply absent, LOCAL_RULE_MISSING.~  - rule 7 / rule 13 (the Global KOS and a Local Addendum give irreconcilable instructions for the same question, so neither can be applied without overriding the other) -^gt! KOS_LOCAL_ADDENDUM_CONFLICT.~  - rule 8 (isStreamlined = TRUE but the conditions for the Domination Methodology are not met - a conflict, a local drill-down requirement, or evidence the rules do not permit it) -^gt! STREAMLINED_NOT_SUPPORTED.~  - §8.3.1 (a STREAMLINED branch was terminated at a non-dominating owner but the 50%-or-less finding itself rests on no stated figure, so the stop is asserted rather than evidenced) -^gt! STREAMLINED_STOP_RULE_NOT_EVIDENCED.~  - rule 11.2 (the client-listed stop rule was APPLIED - all four conditions met, drill-down halted) -^gt! LISTED_ENTITY_STOP_RULE_APPLIED. This is the one flag on this list that records a CORRECT outcome rather than a defect* it makes the stop auditable, and §11.2''s stop is not complete without it.~  - rule 11.2 (drill-','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('down continued past a listed entity where the stop rule was available and permitted, or halted where a local drill-down requirement barred it) -^gt! LISTED_ENTITY_STOP_RULE_BYPASSED.~  - rule 11.2 / 11.3 (a listing or MOS exemption was relied on but the listing evidence is absent, unvalidated, or not bound to the client anchor) -^gt! LISTED_EXEMPTION_NOT_EVIDENCED.~  - rule 11.1 (a regulated-entity exemption was relied on but proof of regulation is absent or not bound to the entity) -^gt! REGULATED_EXEMPTION_NOT_EVIDENCED.~  - rule 11.4 (a government / SOE exemption was relied on but the government-ownership proof is absent or not bound to the entity) -^gt! GOVERNMENT_EXEMPTION_NOT_EVIDENCED.~  - §10.2 (a control indicator from §10.2''s closed list is evidenced on a link that did NOT reach domination under §10.2.0 - a D4 outcome carrying real but insufficient control evidence, which a reviewer must see) -^gt! SIGNIFICANT_CONTROL_INDICATOR.~  EVERY CATEGORY BELOW NOW HAS A TRIGGER, AND THE TRIGGER IS THE ONLY LICENCE TO EMIT IT. A category with no matching condition in this map and no rule naming it is not available* do not reach for a flag because its NAME fits the situation. Reading a name off the category list and emitting it - the failure MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS was emitted through before it had a trigger - is the same run-to-run variance this map exists to remove.~  - INPUT-VALIDATION (a mandatory input missing, blank, or unusable) -^gt! MISSING_MANDATORY_INPUT.~  - rule 11.1.1 / §20 example F (notional UBO fallback cannot be completed) -^gt! NOTIONAL_UBO_ASSESSMENT_REQUIRED! where no natural person was found at all, also NO_NATURAL_PERSON_IDENTIFIED.~  - §20 example D (classification cannot be completed for want of intermediary evidence) -^gt! MISSING_INTERMEDIATE_ENTITY_EVIDENCE.~  - §10.2.0 (a majority is suspected on a link but no percentage is stated and no D1 no-figure wording applies, so the domination ladder had to take D4) -^gt! DOM