tured where evidenced, and §9.2.2''s ladder run on EVERY record so that no actualVotingRightsPercentage is left at an unexplained 0.~  - All conflicts preserved.~  - Local rules applied before classification.~  - Stop rules supported by rule and evidence.~  - No layer skipped.~  - No path collapsed.~  - No external information used.~  - Advisory items generated where required.~  - QA flags generated only for material issues.~  Every exemption, ownership termination decision, streamlined endpoint, or stop rule must reference both documentary evidence and the applicable Global KOS or Local Addenda rule.~  Every advisory item must reference a specific missing document, ownership gap, unresolved conflict, or missing data element.~  Ownership loops or circular ownership structures must be detected, preserved, and not repeatedly traversed.~  ownershipReviewStatus values (emit in clientAnchor.ownershipReviewStatus — OUTPUT-CONTRACT OC.2)*~  - COMPLETE~  - COMPLETE_WITH_QA_FLAGS~  - INCOMPLETE_ADVISORY_REQUIRED','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('~  - NEED_REVIEW~  - DOC_INVALID~  </rule>~~  <rule id="18" priority="HIGH" name="EIGHT-PART REASONING FORMAT">~  For every ownership node and every classification decision, reason must contain eight labeled parts in this order*~  Form is fixed* spell each label exactly as specified, emit the parts in the given order, keep each part on ONE line with no internal line breaks, and emit no text outside the eight labelled parts. Fixed form keeps wording drift from reading as a substantive difference between runs.~  [0] NARRATIVE EXPLANATION~  Provide a concise reviewer-facing narrative explaining*~  - what ownership / control evidence was identified,~  - which document controlled the decision,~  - which supporting or conflicting documents were considered,~  - whether global or streamlined approach was applied,~  - which local overlay / threshold was applied,~  - why the classification was or was not assigned,~  - whether any advisory or QA issue exists.~  [1] OWNERSHIP BASIS~  Required compact format*~  OwnerObserved=[...], OwnedEntity=[.../n-a], RelationshipType=[.../n-a], Layer=[...], DirectOwnershipPercent=[...], OwnershipCodeApplied=[Code*NA / Code*A / Code*B / Code*C / Code*D / Code*E / N/A], VotingRightsPercent=[the figure followed by its §9.2.2 rung in brackets - e.g. 52.27 (deemed) / 52.27 (stated) / 0 (non-voting) / 0 (unknown)! the marker is REQUIRED, a bare figure does not say whether a document supports it], ControlRights=[.../none], DominationIndicator=[YES/NO/n-a], DominationBasis=[D1 majority share ownership / D2 majority voting rights / D3 followed by the named §10.2 basis / none], DominationOwnership=[...], DominationVotingRights=[...], OwnershipApproach=[GLOBAL/STREAMLINED/MIXED/NEED_REVIEW], StopRuleApplied=[.../none], QualifyingInterest=[...], DilutionChain=[the §12.4 percentage-of-percentage chain, every operand AND the result carrying a "%" sign, e.g. 100% × 52.27% = 52.27% / n-a], DominationInheritance=[.../n-a], TargetSum=[.../exempt/n-a], Classification=[the roleCapacity value assigned by the §12.0 ladder, written verbatim as it appears in the schema enum], Conclusion=[...].~  EVERY TOKEN HAS A DEFINED FORM FOR THE LAYER-0 CLIENT RECORD, WHICH ASSERTS NO LINK. Three tokens take the literal "n-a" there and nowhere else - OwnedEntity, RelationshipType and DominationIndicator - because the underlying schema fields are null on that record alone (OC.1) and "null" has no written form on this line. ControlRights takes "none". Do not invent a substitute such as "[none]" for the three "n-a" tokens or "[null]" for any of them* the client record is emitted on every single run, so an undefined token form here is guaranteed run-to-run variance in the one record every consumer reads first. The client record''s full line reads*~  OwnerObserved=[the client legal name], OwnedEntity=[n-a], RelationshipType=[n-a], Layer=[0], DirectOwnershipPercent=[0], OwnershipCodeApplied=[N/A], VotingRightsPercent=[0 (n-a)], ControlRights=[none], Dominatio','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
