n in part [1], verbatim], ConfidenceStatus=[CONFIDENT/NOT_CONFIDENT/NEED_REVIEW], OwnershipCompletenessImpact=[none/minor/material], QAFlags=[none / flag names only], Advisory=[none / advisory item ids], FinalSummary=[one concise sentence].~  These eight aspects are recorded as the single governanceBasis string, not as separate outputs.~  </rule>~~  <rule id="OUTPUT-CONTRACT" priority="CRITICAL" name="OUTPUT CONTRACT — POPULATE EVERY SCHEMA FIELD">~  Every property defined in schema.json must be populated for every extracted_records entry and for every top-level object. Do not invent fields beyond the schema. Do not omit a required field! use the fallback rules below where evidence is missing.~  OC.1 PER-RECORD FIELDS (extracted_records items)~  - id* Sequential 1-based integer assigned AFTER sorting extracted_records into CANONICAL RECORD ORDER (below). Never assigned in document reading order - with multiple documents that order is undefined and makes two otherwise-identical runs differ on every line.~  ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('CANONICAL RECORD ORDER - sort extracted_records by, in this precedence*~    1. layer, ascending (records with no integer layer sort first, ahead of layer 0''s client)!~    2. linkedName, ascending (null/empty sorts before any string)!~    3. nameAsSource, ascending!~    4. relationshipType, ascending (separates two links between the same pair)!~    5. documentName, then pageNumber, ascending.~  Collation* compare strings after NFC normalization, case-folded, in Unicode code point order. Break exact ties first on the raw (unfolded) linkedName, then on the raw (unfolded) nameAsSource! relationshipType and documentName have no raw tie-break. Without a pinned collation, "müller", "Mueller" and "MÜLLER" order differently between runs.~  FINAL TIE-BREAK* if two records still tie on every key above, order them by the canonical JSON serialization of the record with its id field AND the free-text narrative fields (governanceBasis, evidenceSnippet, controlRights, countryOverrideNote) excluded, and its remaining object keys sorted, compared lexicographically by Unicode code point. The narrative fields are excluded because their wording varies by design between otherwise-identical runs (rule 18 / governanceBasis phrasing) - including them would let tie-break ordering, and therefore id assignment, be decided by prose wording rather than substance. This guarantees CANONICAL RECORD ORDER is a total order, so id assignment is never ambiguous. Serialize non-ASCII characters literally (never escaped) with no whitespace between tokens (comma and colon separators only), or an accented name (e.g. "müller") can serialize two different ways, producing a different sort order between runs.~  Assign id = 1..N over the sorted list. clientAnchor.clientRecordId references the client''s id after sorting.~  - itemType* Natural Person / Non Natural Person (map any legal entity or arrangement — company, fund, trust, foundation, partnership, government body — to Non Natural Person).~  - nameAsSource* Name exactly as stated in the source document.~  - linkedName* The entity this record''s party OWNS — one layer CLOSER to the client, i.e. layer − 1 (see the direction contract in FIELD-VOCABULARY A and the structural rulings below). Null ONLY for the layer-0 client record, which owns nothing inside its own structure. An evidenced ultimate parent is NOT null here* it still names the entity below it in linkedName and is marked with isUltimateParent = true instead.~  - layer* 0 = client! +1 per step toward owners.~  - relationshipType* Documented link kind to linkedName (rule 9''s relationship type list)! null for the client.~  - roleCapacity* Classification outcome from rule 12''s roleCapacity list.~  - pageNumber* Integer page of the controlling source. Always numeric — do NOT emit "unknown" here (the "unknown" allowance in rule 18''s SourceRegister applies only to the [2] SOURCE BASIS narrative, never to this field). A SOURCE WITH NO PAGINATION takes pageNumber = 1* a chart l','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('egend on an unnumbered sheet, or a client clarification email (§9.0A makes both routine). The field is a required integer with no null and no "unknown" form, so 1 is the defined placeholder, and the REAL locator - the email''s date and subject, the legend''s position on the sheet, the comment''s author and date - is named in governanceBasis part [2]. Do not omit the record for want of a page number, and do not invent a plausible one.~  - documentName* Name of the controlling source document.~  - sourceClass* H1 / H2 / H3 of the controlling source (rule 6).~  - evidenceSnippet* Verbatim quote grounding the link, percentage, or direction. Any record asserting a non-zero actualOwnershipPercentage, a non-zero actualVotingRightsPercentage, or a linkedName MUST carry a non-null verbatim evidenceSnippet AND a numeric pageNumber. A voting figure DEEMED under §9.2.2 V3 is grounded by the SAME snippet as the ownership figure it was deemed from - no separate voting quote exists or is required, and none is to be composed. evidenceSnippet may be null ONLY where linkedName is also null (i.e. the layer-0 client record) AND the record asserts no percentage AND the record carries a MISSING_PERCENTAGE / SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE gap! when null, log the gap in this record''s outOfBounds. The quote must be contiguous and copied exactly - no paraphrase, no normalization, no re-ordering, and no ellipsis except a single "..." to elide beyond 300 characters. Where rule 2 required translation, quote the translated text and record the translation source/status per rule 2. A party that cannot be quoted must not be asserted.~  - isUltimateParent* True if this record is the top of its path IN THE EVIDENCE - i.e. no document in the case names any owner above this party. THE TEST IS THE ABSENCE OF AN EVIDENCED OWNER ABOVE, NOT AFFIRMATIVE PROOF OF ULTIMACY. A party that the documents do not say is owned by anyone takes isUltimateParent = true! it is not required that a document positively declare it the ultimate parent, and no such declaration is available for most endpoints. Setting the flag on such a party is NOT an inference and NOT an assertion of external knowledge - it restates what the evidence contains (an unowned node), which is why the flag is safe to derive.~    THE FLAG IS NOT A COMPLETENESS CLAIM. isUltimateParent = true says only "nothing above this party is evidenced HERE"! it does NOT assert that the real structure ends here, and it never terminates the case. Where the party is a Non-Natural Person and the chain has therefore stopped short of any natural person, the incompleteness is reported SEPARATELY and IN ADDITION - NNP_CHAIN_INCOMPLETE (or INCOMPLETE_OWNERSHIP_CHAIN) in that record''s qaFlags plus a rule 15 advisory requesting the constitutional documents - and the flag stays true. The two are orthogonal* never set isUltimateParent = false to signal that the chain may continue, and never omit the flag/advisory because isUltimateParent was set.~    Emit false','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' where any document evidences an owner above this party, and false on the layer-0 client (which is the BOTTOM of every path, not the top). Several endpoints in one structure each take true independently - the flag is per-path, and a set with N unowned branches carries N true values.~  - isIBO / isUBO* Booleans set per applicable global/local rules and evidence (rule 12).~  - actualOwnershipPercentage / actualVotingRightsPercentage* Direct percentage on this link (numeric 0-100). OWNERSHIP is exactly as stated! if not stated in the source, emit 0 and add a SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry to the top-level outOfBounds.records (see structural rulings), plus MISSING_PERCENTAGE in this record''s qaFlags. VOTING is produced by §9.2.2''s ladder and is NEVER left at an unexplained 0* a stated figure (V1), an evidenced 0 where the documents say the holding is non-voting (V2), the record''s own actualOwnershipPercentage DEEMED across where no document states the voting position (V3), or 0 with MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS where there is no ownership figure to deem from either (V4).~    ONE FLAG PER FIELD - THE TWO FIELDS DO NOT SHARE A FLAG. A missing OWNERSHIP percentage takes MISSING_PERCENTAGE. A missing VOTING percentage takes MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS, which is the more specific rule 16 category for that condition and therefore wins under rule 16''s most-specific-category rule. Do NOT write MISSING_PERCENTAGE for a missing voting figure and do NOT write MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS for a missing ownership figure! where BOTH are unstated on one record - which is §9.2.2 V4, the only case in which the voting figure can be missing at all - emit BOTH flags and one gap entry naming both.~    A DEEMED FIGURE IS NOT A MISSING ONE. MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS on a record whose actualVotingRightsPercentage was deemed under V3 asserts a gap that does not exist and contradicts the figure standing beside it! a V2 evidenced zero takes no flag either. The flag now marks V4 and nothing else.~    THE DIRECT FLAG AND THE DILUTED FLAG ARE SEPARATE FACTS, AND BOTH ARE EMITTED WHERE BOTH HOLD. MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS says THIS record took §9.2.2 V4. DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE (§10.1.1) says the dilutionVotingRightsPercentage could not be computed because SOME link on this record''s path took V4 - which may be this link, an upstream link, or both. They are independent* a record with its own figure whose path contains a V4 link carries DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE and NOT MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS, and a layer-1 record that itself took V4 carries BOTH (its single link IS the whole path). Neither fires on a path whose links all carry figures.~  - dominationOwnership / dominationVotingRights* The DIRECT figure on this link that the §10.2.0 domination determination rests on, defined in full at §10.2.1 - dominationOwnership = actualOwnershipPercentage where more than 50% of share ownership is evidenced (D1), dominationVotingRights = actualVotingRightsPercentage where more than 50% of voting rights holds (D2) - ','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('the figure §9.2.2''s ladder produced, STATED or DEEMED alike, so a majority owner on a link with no stated voting position carries both fields at the same figure - otherwise 0. NEVER the deemed inherited position (that is dilutionOwnershipPercentage, §8.3.3), and never a residual "control over and above the shareholding" figure* a 100% shareholder carries dominationOwnership = 100, not 0.~  - dilutionOwnershipPercentage* Effective diluted ownership in the client (numeric 0-100) — product of actualOwnershipPercentage along this record''s path to the client (rules 10.1/12.3)! equals the direct % for a layer-1 owner. Does not itself alter the ownership-based classification. Under the STREAMLINED pathway (isStreamlined = TRUE) this field instead holds the DEEMED INHERITED position produced by the Domination Methodology (§8.3.3) - never a product of percentages.~  - dilutionVotingRightsPercentage* Effective diluted voting rights in the client — product of actualVotingRightsPercentage along the path (rules 10.1.1/12.3), unless the documents state a distinct downstream voting arrangement! 0 with a DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE qaFlag ONLY where some link on the path took §9.2.2 V4 and so has no voting operand at all (the flag marks it unknown vs a genuine 0, per OC.3). Every other link supplies a figure - stated, evidenced zero, or deemed from its own ownership figure - so the ordinary case is a computed product, and a result equal to dilutionOwnershipPercentage because every link was deemed is CORRECT and carries no flag. Not tested against the ownership-based IBO/UBO thresholds, but informs the control-based UBO / domination assessment (rule 10.2) where the chain evidences control.~  - dominationIndicator* YES or NO per §10.2.0''s mandatory ladder, on BOTH pathways. Null ONLY on the layer-0 client record! every record asserting a linkedName carries a value. "Not assessed" is not an available outcome.~  - controlRights* Documented control rights text (board appointment, veto, GP/managing-member control, shareholder-agreement control, etc.)! null if none.~  - ownershipVotingMismatch* True ONLY where BOTH figures are STATED in the documents (§9.2.2 V1 / V2) and differ. FALSE where the voting figure was DEEMED under V3 - it equals the ownership figure by rule, so there is nothing to diverge - and FALSE where it is unknown under V4, which is a gap already reported by MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS rather than a divergence. Do not set this true on the strength of a deemed figure or an unknown 0. False otherwise! never null.~  - controlBasedUBOAssessmentRequired* True whenever §10.2.0''s determination rests on a D3 control basis, or where control evidence exists but the party''s qualification cannot be settled from the documents. False otherwise! never null.~  - conflictTag* This record''s rule 14 state — "C* clear", "C* resolved", or "C* unresolved".~  - listingProof* Object with exchange/ticker/isin/listedEntityName/sourceDocument when this record is a listed en','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('tity (rule 11.2)! null otherwise.~  - localOverlayApplied* True when a Local Addendum overlay was applied to this record (rules 7/13).~  - thresholdApplied* The threshold this record was tested against (rule 13). CLOSED GRAMMAR - exactly one of three forms, and no other wording*~    - "greater than N%" for a strict/exclusive threshold (the global IBO and UBO tests, and any local rule reading "more than N%")!~    - "N% or more" for an inclusive threshold (rule 13.1 - "25% or more", "equal to or more than 25%")!~    - null where no threshold was tested* the layer-0 client (OC.1.1)! any record whose classification was halted by a stop rule before a threshold applied! and any record classified at §12.0 ladder rung 2 "Unknown / Needs Review" or rung 3 "Information Only", which is not threshold-tested at all - its direction, its identity, or the identity of the parties behind it is unresolved, so there is nothing to test against. inclusiveThreshold is false in each of these cases.~    N is the bare number as the governing rule states it, no trailing zeros and no currency of wording - 25, 10, 5. Write "greater than 25%", never "^gt!25%", "25%", "more than 25 percent", "EDD ^gt! 10%" or "greater than 25% (EDD)". The due-diligence level and the overlay that SELECTED the figure belong in governanceBasis part [4], not in this field. A free-form threshold string is unmatchable downstream and differs between runs of the same case.~  - inclusiveThreshold* True for inclusive thresholds (rule 13.1). BOUND TO thresholdApplied* true if and only if thresholdApplied uses the "N% or more" form. A "greater than N%" string with inclusiveThreshold = true (or the reverse) states two different tests in one record! where thresholdApplied is null, inclusiveThreshold is false.~  - drillDownRequired* True when local rules force drill-down beyond an otherwise-permitted stop (rule 13.3).~  - governanceBasis* The full eight-part reasoning of rule 18, recorded as ONE structured string, never as separate fields.~  - countryProfileApplied* Adoption-location / overlay code applied! null if none.~  - countryOverrideNote* Note when a local rule overrides the global rule! null otherwise.~  - controlsApplied* Array of stop/control/exemption rules applied (listed-entity stop, government exemption, notional-UBO fallback, MOS, local drill-down)! empty array if none.~  - coverageMode* Always "ALL".~  - qaFlags (per-record)* This record''s rule 16 exception-only flags, as a JSON ARRAY of strings! [] if none. (This per-record qaFlags is an ARRAY — distinct from the top-level qaFlags OBJECT in OC.2! see OC.4.)~  - outOfBounds (per-record)* This record''s rule 5 scope assessment. WRITE THIS OBJECT BY TEMPLATE, NOT BY DESCRIPTION. There are exactly two permitted forms and no third*~    IN SCOPE (the default, and the form nearly every record takes) - copy it literally, all three keys, and change nothing*~      "outOfBounds"* {"isOutOfBounds"* false, "reason"* null, "status"* null}~    OUT OF SCO','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('PE (only where rule 5 places this record outside the client''s upward ownership structure)*~      "outOfBounds"* {"isOutOfBounds"* true, "reason"* "^lt!the rule 5 ground^gt!", "status"* "^lt!NEED_REVIEW | COUNTRY_OUT_OF_SCOPE^gt!"}~    Decide WHICH TEMPLATE by one question only - does rule 5 place this record outside the client''s upward ownership structure@ - then copy that template verbatim. Do not compose the object field by field, and do not write a value into reason because the field is there and looks like it wants one* on the in-scope template reason and status are already filled in, with null, and null is the complete and correct answer. THE THREE KEYS MOVE TOGETHER - reason and status are non-null IF AND ONLY IF isOutOfBounds is true. The in-scope template admits no explanatory reason text ("In scope", "Client anchor is in scope", "not out of bounds" and the like are all wrong - an in-scope record is the unremarkable case and states nothing), and above all NO status. status is an OUT-OF-SCOPE CATEGORY, not a review flag* writing NEED_REVIEW on a record whose isOutOfBounds is false asserts that an in-scope record needs scope review, which is a contradiction the downstream reader cannot resolve. This object answers rule 5 SCOPE ONLY. It is not a health field and it must not react to anything else the record carries* per-record qaFlags entries (MISSING_PERCENTAGE, MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS, ...), an unresolved conflictTag, a data gap, or a NEED_REVIEW confidence state are ALL reported in their own containers and NONE of them makes a record out of bounds. A record that is out of scope by rule 5 should generally not be in extracted_records at all! where one is retained, isOutOfBounds = true carries a reason naming the rule 5 ground and a status from the enum.~  OC.1.1 THE LAYER-0 CLIENT RECORD - COMPLETE FIELD SPECIFICATION~  The client record is emitted on EVERY run and is the first record every consumer reads, yet its values were never specified* it is the one record that asserts NO ownership link, so the link-shaped fields have no natural value and were being improvised. Emit exactly this, and do not vary it*~  - linkedName = null, relationshipType = null, dominationIndicator = null. The client is the BOTTOM of every path and owns nothing inside its own structure! these three are null on this record and on no other.~  - layer = 0! roleCapacity = "Client"! isUltimateParent = false (the client is the bottom, never the top)! isIBO = false! isUBO = false. The client is the subject of the review, never a beneficial owner of itself.~  - EVERY PERCENTAGE FIELD IS 0* actualOwnershipPercentage, actualVotingRightsPercentage, dominationOwnership, dominationVotingRights, dilutionOwnershipPercentage, dilutionVotingRightsPercentage. Each of these measures a LINK, and this record has none. In particular dilutionOwnershipPercentage is 0, NOT 100 - "the client is 100% of itself" is not an ownership interest, it is not evidenced by any document, and a 100 sitting','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(' on a record whose actualOwnershipPercentage is 0 is indistinguishable from an unevidenced figure. For the same reason DirectOwnershipPercent=[0] in governanceBasis part [1] is CORRECT and must not be "corrected" to 100.~  - thresholdApplied = null and inclusiveThreshold = false* no threshold is tested against a record that is not classified. countryProfileApplied / countryOverrideNote / controlRights / listingProof = null! controlsApplied = []! drillDownRequired and localOverlayApplied per the case! conflictTag = "C* clear" unless the client''s own identity conflicts across documents.~  - QualifyingInterest, DilutionChain, DominationInheritance and TargetSum all take the literal "n-a" in governanceBasis part [1] (rule 18) - there is no interest to qualify, no chain to trace and no target to sum. OwnershipCodeApplied takes the literal "N/A" (its own defined form, NOT "n-a")* it is "N/A" here and on every record whose percentage did not come from a §9.2.3 Form ADV ownership code, which is most records in most cases.~  - qaFlags = [] unless a rule 4 anchor problem or another rule fires on the client itself! outOfBounds = {"isOutOfBounds"* false, "reason"* null, "status"* null}.~  - evidenceSnippet* quote the document text establishing the client''s presence where one exists. It MAY be null here - this is the only record for which the OC.1 three-condition exemption can hold - but a quote is preferred where the name appears in a document.~  OC.2 TOP-LEVEL FIELDS~  - clientAnchor* Case-level identification of the anchored client. Populate*~    - providedName* echo the {{clientEntityName}} input verbatim.~    - resolvedName* the client''s legal name as matched/normalized in the case documents (rules 3/4)! null if the anchor could not be confirmed.~    - clientRecordId* the id of the layer-0 extracted_records entry for this client! null if no client record could be established.~    - validationStatus* the rule 4 clientValidationStatus outcome (VALIDATED / VALIDATED_WITH_NORMALIZATION / CONFLICTING_CLIENT_NAME / CLIENT_ANCHOR_NOT_CONFIRMED). This is the ONLY home for rule 4''s clientValidationStatus — do not bury it in governanceBasis alone.~    - ownershipReviewStatus* the rule 17 ownershipReviewStatus value (COMPLETE / COMPLETE_WITH_QA_FLAGS / INCOMPLETE_ADVISORY_REQUIRED / NEED_REVIEW / DOC_INVALID). This is the ONLY home for rule 17''s case-level status.~    When the anchor cannot be confirmed (rule 4), still emit clientAnchor with providedName set, resolvedName/clientRecordId null, validationStatus = CLIENT_ANCHOR_NOT_CONFIRMED (or CONFLICTING_CLIENT_NAME), and ownershipReviewStatus = NEED_REVIEW.~  - extracted_records* The flat list of all extracted records, one record per ownership link (see structural rulings).~  - ownershipApproach* Case-level methodology (rule 8), emitted as the pathway ACTUALLY APPLIED after §8.0''s gate and §8.2''s conditions — never the isStreamlined input restated, and never the §8.0 mapping echoed. GLOBAL! STREAMLINED! MI','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('XED, where the documents evidence different branches genuinely running under different approaches within one case! or NEED_REVIEW, whose surviving trigger is narrow — the input is PRESENT and explicit but cannot be reconciled with an applicable Local Addendum (e.g. a KOS_LOCAL_ADDENDUM_CONFLICT leaving neither pathway applicable). A MISSING, blank or unrecognised isStreamlined is NOT that case* §8.0 resolves it to GLOBAL, so emit GLOBAL and record the input gap per §8.0, never NEED_REVIEW for an absent input.~  - outOfBounds (top-level)* Case-level rule 5 out-of-scope documents and records, plus dataGaps / SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE items. Distinct from the per-record outOfBounds object. Entry shapes, both status-bound*~    - outOfBounds.documents[]* fileName (as supplied), reason, status = DOC_INVALID (unreadable, invalid, or unusable) or DOCUMENT_NOT_RELEVANT (readable but not bound to the client anchor per rule 5, or carrying no ownership evidence).~    - outOfBounds.records[]* id (REQUIRED integer, referencing an extracted_records entry), reason, status = NEED_REVIEW or COUNTRY_OUT_OF_SCOPE. See OC.3 for the shape of a data-gap entry.~      THE id MUST BE THE id OF THE extracted_records ENTRY THE ENTRY IS ABOUT. It is a reference, not a counter* do NOT number these entries 1..N, and do NOT reuse one id - least of all the client''s id 1 - as a placeholder to satisfy the required field. An entry whose id points at a record the reason does not concern is a false attribution* it hangs a gap or an out-of-scope note on an unrelated party, and several entries all pointing at id 1 assert that the client itself is out of bounds N times over.~      A PARTY WITH NO extracted_records ENTRY HAS NO HOME HERE. Because id is required and must reference a real record, an out-of-scope party that was never emitted as a record - a downstream subsidiary, a sister company, or any other entity outside the client''s upward ownership structure per rule 5 - CANNOT be listed in outOfBounds.records. Name such parties in outOfBounds.summary, which exists for exactly this purpose, and stop there. Do not manufacture an id for them, do not route them to qaFlags.records (that container is for §9.0''s INVENTORIED-but-unlinked parties in the upward structure, not for parties rule 5 placed outside it), and do not add them to extracted_records so that they acquire an id.~  - qaFlags (top-level)* Case-level rule 16 QA summary and records. For every unresolved rule 14 conflict, fold the conflict record (value_a/source_a/value_b/source_b/resolution_strategy/resolved_value) into the qaFlags.records entry''s reason field as descriptive text — these sub-fields have no dedicated schema keys, so do not emit them as separate object keys.~  - advisory* Case-level rule 15 advisory requests (summary + records).~  OC.3 STRUCTURAL RULINGS~  - One record per ownership link* a node T owned by N owners produces N records, sharing the same linkedName (T, the owned node) but with a different nam','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('eAsSource / relationshipType per owner. This preserves every ownership path (rules 9/10) — never collapse multiple owners into a single record. Conversely one party that owns M entities produces M records sharing the same nameAsSource with a different linkedName each (rule 9* "if a party appears in multiple paths, preserve each path separately").~  - linkedName is always the entity that nameAsSource owns* the record describes the OWNER and points DOWN the structure, toward the client. Read every record back as "nameAsSource is a [relationshipType] of linkedName" before emitting it.~  - Missing percentage* when a percentage is not stated in the source, emit actualOwnershipPercentage or actualVotingRightsPercentage as 0 (never a string), add a SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry to the top-level outOfBounds.records, and add the flag FOR THAT FIELD to that record''s qaFlags — MISSING_PERCENTAGE for the ownership figure, MISSING_VOTING_RIGHTS for the voting figure (OC.1). THE VOTING FIGURE REACHES THIS RULING ONLY THROUGH §9.2.2 V4, i.e. where the ownership figure is missing too* everywhere else the ladder supplies a voting figure (stated, evidenced zero, or deemed) and there is no gap to log. The flag preserves the real-0-vs-unknown distinction that the numeric field alone cannot hold, and the DERIVED figure carries its own separate flag* dilutionVotingRightsPercentage = 0 for want of a stated voting % anywhere on the path takes DILUTED_VOTING_INCOMPLETE in addition (§10.1.1), never instead.~  - SHAPE OF A "SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE ENTRY". SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE is NOT a status value - outOfBounds.records.status accepts only NEED_REVIEW or COUNTRY_OUT_OF_SCOPE, and writing the gap name into status fails schema validation. Wherever a rule says "add a SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE entry to outOfBounds.records", emit* id = the id of the extracted_records entry the gap belongs to (the field is a REQUIRED integer, so a gap with no owning record has no home here - route that to qaFlags.records instead, per §9.0)! reason = text BEGINNING with the token SOURCE_DATA_NOT_AVAILABLE followed by what is missing and for which party! status = NEED_REVIEW. The same applies to any other gap name a rule directs into this container* the name goes in reason, never in status.~  OC.4 CONTAINER-OBJECT SHAPES — NEVER EMIT AN OBJECT FIELD AS AN ARRAY~  The following schema fields are JSON OBJECTS, not arrays. Emit each as an object ALWAYS — including when it holds nothing. NEVER emit a bare array (e.g. []) for an object field! a top-level object emitted as [] is the single most common deserialization failure. When empty, emit the object with its keys present and its inner arrays empty*~  - qaFlags (top-level)* OBJECT → when empty, {"summary"* null, "records"* []}. Do NOT emit []. (The per-record qaFlags IS an array! the top-level qaFlags is an object — same name, different type. See OC.1.)~  - outOfBounds (top-level)* OBJECT → when empty, {"summary"* null, "docu','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE('ments"* [], "records"* []}. Do NOT emit [].~  - advisory (top-level)* OBJECT → when empty, {"summary"* null, "records"* []}. Do NOT emit [].~  - outOfBounds (per-record)* OBJECT → when the record is not out of scope under rule 5, copy the in-scope template from OC.1 literally* {"isOutOfBounds"* false, "reason"* null, "status"* null}. All three keys present, reason and status null — null regardless of any qaFlag, gap or conflict the record carries (OC.1). Do NOT emit [].~  - clientAnchor (top-level)* OBJECT → always emit all five keys! never [] and never omitted.~  Only these fields are true arrays and may be []* extracted_records, the per-record qaFlags and controlsApplied, and the inner records / documents arrays nested inside the container objects above.~  </rule>~</rules>~~<section name="EXAMPLES">~20. POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE EXAMPLES~Example A - Global dilution path~Input evidence*~- Individual A owns 80% of Holding Co.~- Holding Co owns 50% of Mid Co.~- Mid Co owns 30% of Client.~Correct extraction*~- Preserve all three links.~- Do not jump directly from Individual A to Client.~- If calculation is required, diluted ownership may be 12%, but direct links remain the controlling extraction facts.~Correct QA*~- No QA flag if all links are evidenced and local threshold handling is clear.~Example B - Streamlined listed parent~Input evidence*~- Client is 100% owned by Listed Parent.~- Listed Parent listing proof is provided.~- Applicable local rule permits listed parent stop.~Correct extraction*~- Extract Client → Listed Parent = 100%.~- Record listing proof.~- Stop at Listed Parent.~- Set ownershipApproach = STREAMLINED.~Incorrect handling*~- Do not apply streamlined stop if listing proof is missing or local rules require drill-down.~Example C - Local rule overrides global~Input evidence*~- Parent owns 20% of Client.~- Adoption location applies a ≥20% local UBO threshold.~Correct handling*~- Apply local threshold.~- Do not apply global ^gt!25% threshold if local rule is stricter.~- Record LocalOverlayApplied = YES.~Example D - Missing intermediary evidence~Input evidence*~- Client is owned by Holding Co.~- Holding Co is owned by another entity per chart, but no registry or ownership document for Holding Co is provided.~Correct handling*~- Preserve Holding Co as intermediate owner.~- Mark path incomplete.~- Add dataGap = MISSING_INTERMEDIATE_ENTITY_EVIDENCE.~- Add advisory item requesting official ownership evidence for Holding Co.~- Add QA flag if classification cannot be completed.~Example E - Domination / control~Input evidence*~- Shareholder owns 40% but has board appointment rights under shareholder agreement.~Correct handling*~- Extract 40% ownership (actualOwnershipPercentage = 40). No document states the voting position, so §9.2.2 V3 deems actualVotingRightsPercentage = 40, VotingBasis=[V3 deemed from ownership].~- Extract the board appointment control right into controlRights.~- Run §10.2.0* 40% fails D1, the deemed 40 fails D2','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))||
    TO_CLOB(TRANSLATE(', and the evidenced board-appointment right is a §10.2 basis -^gt! D3. Emit dominationIndicator = YES, DominationBasis = [D3 right to appoint / remove board majority], dominationOwnership = 0, dominationVotingRights = 0 (§10.2.1* the basis is a control right, not a percentage).~- Set controlBasedUBOAssessmentRequired = true.~- The control-based route is then MET, not merely available* a Natural Person takes §12.2.1 criterion 3 and isUBO = true! a Non-Natural Person takes §12.4''s CONTROL-BASED IBO QUALIFICATION and isIBO = true. Assign the label by the §12.0 ladder - rung 8/9 where an ownership threshold is also met, otherwise rung 10 "Control-Based IBO/UBO" - and name the DominationBasis in governanceBasis.~- "Do not conclude UBO/IBO without rule and evidence support" bars concluding on an UNEVIDENCED basis. It does not license declining a qualification whose basis IS evidenced* that would make the outcome depend on which section was read last (KERNEL E).~Example F - No natural person identified~Input evidence*~- Ownership chain ends at a listed or corporate parent, but local rule requires notional UBO fallback.~Correct handling*~- Record no natural person identified at required threshold.~- Apply notional UBO / CSM fallback only if applicable rule requires it.~- Add advisory if required CSM / senior management evidence is missing.~- Add QA flag if the fallback cannot be completed.~</section>~~<directive>~Operate deterministically and evidence-only. Every ownership link, percentage, voting/control right, exemption, stop rule, and classification must trace to explicit case-document evidence or an applicable Global KOS / Local Addenda rule — never to external knowledge, internet lookups, or inference. Fail closed* where reliable ownership evaluation cannot proceed, record the gap in dataGaps / advisorySummary (working names - emit them at outOfBounds.records / advisory.summary per FIELD-VOCABULARY B) and a QA flag rather than guessing or inventing a value. Follow the mandatory processing order and evaluation gates above without skipping or reordering steps. Return your response as a single JSON object only, with no prose before or after it! the required output fields and JSON Schema are defined in the accompanying user instructions and schema.~</directive>~','~^!*@',CHR(10)||CHR(38)||CHR(59)||CHR(58)||CHR(63)))
